<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Sign in with Apple.

	  App Store rule 4.8 requires it wherever an app offers another
	  third-party sign-in, and ZRP offers Google. It was held back while
	  the backend had no way to take a native credential: the server
	  registered Apple only as a NextAuth *web* provider using a Services
	  ID, and no route accepted an ASAuthorizationAppleIDCredential.

	  That is no longer true. POST /api/mobile/auth/apple verifies the
	  identity token against Apple's published JWKS - issuer, audience,
	  expiry, signature and the per-attempt nonce - and mints the same
	  NextAuth session token the password and Google logins return. The
	  app cannot function without this entitlement declared, so it is
	  declared.

	  Still required OUTSIDE this repository, and it cannot be done from
	  here: "Sign In with Apple" must be enabled for the one.zrp.social
	  App ID in the Apple Developer portal. Until it is, a *signed* build
	  will fail to provision - an unsigned CI build is unaffected.
	-->
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>

	<!--
	  Push notifications + PushKit VoIP (Task #6).

	  The client-side wiring is real and complete: AppDelegate registers
	  for remote notifications, PushCoordinator/VoipPushCoordinator
	  handle the device token and VoIP token lifecycles, and
	  src/lib/apns.ts is a real, direct HTTP/2 APNs sender (not FCM - see
	  that file's own doc comment for why this app never needed the
	  Firebase iOS SDK or a GoogleService-Info.plist at all).

	  "development" here, matching how Xcode's own template generates
	  this key: a signed Debug/TestFlight build talks to APNs' sandbox
	  environment, and archiving for App Store distribution has Xcode
	  substitute "production" automatically from the distribution
	  provisioning profile - this file's own value is never what ships.

	  Same real-world gap as Sign In with Apple above: "aps-environment"
	  and the "Push Notifications"/"Background Modes: Voice over IP"
	  capabilities must be enabled for the one.zrp.social App ID in the
	  Apple Developer portal, and real APNS_KEY_ID/APNS_TEAM_ID/
	  APNS_BUNDLE_ID/APNS_PRIVATE_KEY values (a real .p8 key) configured
	  server-side, before this is live end to end - neither exists yet
	  (no Apple Developer account for this app at all - see above). A
	  *signed* build will fail to provision until then; the unsigned CI
	  build this repo runs today is unaffected. See ios-native/PARITY.md.
	-->
	<key>aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>

	<!--
	  NOT declared yet, deliberately:

	  com.apple.developer.associated-domains (universal links) needs
	  public/.well-known/apple-app-site-association to name
	  "TEAMID.one.zrp.social". The Team ID does not exist yet - there is
	  no Apple Developer account for this app - and an invented one
	  produces a file Apple silently refuses to honour, which is worse
	  than no file at all. The app's own half is done: DeepLink.swift maps
	  every ZRP web path this app has a screen for, and the tab shell
	  opens them. When the Team ID exists, add:

	      <key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	      <array><string>applinks:zrp.one</string></array>

	  Android's equivalent (public/.well-known/assetlinks.json) is real
	  because its signing certificate exists.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
